# Sagaverse requests. Run them from IntelliJ's HTTP client, or copy them as curl commands.
# Prerequisite: `make up`, then the three services (dev mode: ./mvnw -pl <svc> spring-boot:run).
# Ports: order 8081, payment 8082, inventory 8083.

### 1. Happy path: charge 42.50, reserve 2 x SKU-1, order ends CONFIRMED
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "cust-1", "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 2, "amount": 42.50}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.orderId); %}

### 2. Watch the saga: status, saga.state, saga.transitions
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{orderId}}

### 3. Invalid request: 400, no saga started
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "cust-1", "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 0, "amount": 42.50}

### 4. Unknown order: 404
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/does-not-exist

### 5. F1 payment declined: amount above payment.decline-amount-over (1000.00 in dev) -> CANCELLED / FAILED
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "cust-1", "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 1, "amount": 5000.00}

> {% client.global.set("declinedOrderId", response.body.orderId); %}

###
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{declinedOrderId}}

### 6. F2 out of stock: charged, then refunded -> CANCELLED / COMPENSATED (SKU-EMPTY has 0 units)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "cust-1", "sku": "SKU-EMPTY", "quantity": 1, "amount": 10.00}

> {% client.global.set("oosOrderId", response.body.orderId); %}

###
GET http://localhost:8081/orders/{{oosOrderId}}

### Health of each service
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health

###
GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/health

###
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health

# Coming in later phases: duplicate delivery and crash scenarios (Phases 4-5).
